% expect-output: {10.0 10.0 90.0 90.0 setbbox 10.0 10.0 moveto 90.0 90.0 lineto closepath}
% Scenario: a user path round-trips. The first page fills a literal
% user path with ufill; the second fills the same points built by hand,
% and the two pages dump identically. Appending the user path with
% uappend and reading it back with false upath gives an executable
% array headed by the path's own bounding box and setbbox, with real
% coordinates in the current user space.
/tri {0 0 100 100 setbbox 10 10 moveto 90 90 lineto closepath} cvlit def
tri ufill
showpage
10 10 moveto 90 90 lineto closepath fill
showpage
newpath tri uappend false upath ==
